# Copy to .env.prod and fill in your real domain before deploying.
# Point the DNS record (A/AAAA) at the VPS's IP before starting the stack,
# otherwise Traefik (the shared reverse proxy already running on the VPS —
# see docker-compose.prod.yml) will fail to obtain a Let's Encrypt
# certificate for it.
#
# Single-domain setup: Traefik routes /api, /admin and /uploads to the
# backend by path and everything else to the frontend — no separate
# api. subdomain needed. Swap this for the real domain once it's bought
# and pointed (e.g. www.interformci.com).
#
# NOTE: the bare `srv1896005.hstgr.cloud` hostname is already claimed by
# another project on this shared VPS (jaures) — using it here causes a
# Traefik Host() collision where requests silently land on the wrong app.
# `*.srv1896005.hstgr.cloud` is wildcarded by Hostinger, so a distinct
# subdomain (below) resolves fine and avoids the collision.

DOMAIN=interformci.srv1896005.hstgr.cloud
